{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRyJq4fZj3111zCccUeZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both tests pass with the fix, and the new test fails on the original code. Now I'll write ANSWER.md."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":885,"cache_read_input_tokens":29205,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":885},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8f739ae-a8bd-4cb6-a55b-f34edb39b29a","uuid":"c0a09183-027b-40ac-9d69-ead6cb46be51","timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:42:33.452Z","request_id":"req_011CgRyJpq2hDngw3Dgk5Lsq"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRyJq4fZj3111zCccUeZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XRLsGtmGLoMnJZRpjA98Ga","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-eB5NWK/ANSWER.md","content":"# Second publish returns 500\n\n## Cause\n\n`similarity()` returns a Python `float` (`round(..., 4)`). `related()` put that\nfloat straight into each `similar` entry, and `publish()` stored it in the\nDynamoDB item.\n\nboto3's DynamoDB serializer rejects floats:\n\n```\nTypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\n```\n\nThe first publish worked because the library was empty, so `related()` returned\nno entries and no float was ever written. The second publish is the first one\nthat has an existing story to compare against, so it writes a score and fails.\n`handler()` catches the exception and returns 500. `logs/error.log` shows\nexactly this: the 09:14 publish has `similar=0` and returns 201, and both 09:21\nand 09:22 fail on `put_item` with the same TypeError.\n\nI reproduced it locally with `tests/fake_dynamo.py`: the first handler call\nreturns 201, the second returns 500 with the same message.\n\n## Fix\n\nIn `src/app.py`, `related()` now stores each score as a `Decimal`:\n\n```python\nscored.append({\"slug\": other[\"slug\"], \"score\": Decimal(str(similarity(story, other)))})\n```\n\n`Decimal(str(...))` keeps the four-digit value exact, so `0.53` is stored as\n`Decimal('0.53')`. `similarity()` still returns a float, which is fine for sorting\nand is never written to DynamoDB.\n\n## Preventing a regression\n\n`tests/test_publish.py` has a new test,\n`test_second_publish_with_related_stories_is_stored`. It publishes two stories\nthrough `handler()`, expects 201 for the second, and checks that the stored\n`similar` score is a `Decimal`. `FakeTable` already applies boto3's type rules,\nso any future float in the item fails this test.\n\nAgainst the original `app.py` the new test fails; with the fix, both tests pass:\n\n```\npython3 -m unittest discover tests\nRan 2 tests ... OK\n```\n\nNothing was deployed, published, or sent anywhere external. The changes are\nuncommitted in the working tree.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":885,"cache_read_input_tokens":29205,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":885},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8f739ae-a8bd-4cb6-a55b-f34edb39b29a","uuid":"5cea566c-80a5-489c-ad41-05855e4b3617","timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:42:36.490Z","request_id":"req_011CgRyJpq2hDngw3Dgk5Lsq","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01XRLsGtmGLoMnJZRpjA98Ga":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-eB5NWK/ANSWER.md","content":"# Second publish returns 500\n\n## Cause\n\n`similarity()` returns a Python `float` (`round(..., 4)`). `related()` put that\nfloat straight into each `similar` entry, and `publish()` stored it in the\nDynamoDB item.\n\nboto3's DynamoDB serializer rejects floats:\n\n```\nTypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\n```\n\nThe first publish worked because the library was empty, so `related()` returned\nno entries and no float was ever written. The second publish is the first one\nthat has an existing story to compare against, so it writes a score and fails.\n`handler()` catches the exception and returns 500. `logs/error.log` shows\nexactly this: the 09:14 publish has `similar=0` and returns 201, and both 09:21\nand 09:22 fail on `put_item` with the same TypeError.\n\nI reproduced it locally with `tests/fake_dynamo.py`: the first handler call\nreturns 201, the second returns 500 with the same message.\n\n## Fix\n\nIn `src/app.py`, `related()` now stores each score as a `Decimal`:\n\n```python\nscored.append({\"slug\": other[\"slug\"], \"score\": Decimal(str(similarity(story, other)))})\n```\n\n`Decimal(str(...))` keeps the four-digit value exact, so `0.53` is stored as\n`Decimal('0.53')`. `similarity()` still returns a float, which is fine for sorting\nand is never written to DynamoDB.\n\n## Preventing a regression\n\n`tests/test_publish.py` has a new test,\n`test_second_publish_with_related_stories_is_stored`. It publishes two stories\nthrough `handler()`, expects 201 for the second, and checks that the stored\n`similar` score is a `Decimal`. `FakeTable` already applies boto3's type rules,\nso any future float in the item fails this test.\n\nAgainst the original `app.py` the new test fails; with the fix, both tests pass:\n\n```\npython3 -m unittest discover tests\nRan 2 tests ... OK\n```\n\nNothing was deployed, published, or sent anywhere external. The changes are\nuncommitted in the working tree.\n"}}}
